	(text "A1 expansion connector (UG130 table 13-2): shared with the board's SRAM\n5-19 odd: IC10 IO0-IO7 (sram_d[7:0]); A0-A17: pins 6, 8, 10, 12, 14,\n24, 23, 26, 25, 28, 27, 30, 29, 32, 31, 34, 33, 35; 16 WE#, 18 OE#\n21 M7 ROM_CE (unshared), 20 P9 ROM_A18 (DOUT/BUSY: toggles while the FPGA\nconfigures, harmless on an address line); free: 4 N8, 22 M10\n36-40: JTAG (TMS, TCK, TDO): do not connect"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 245 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "05f1e9ef-5026-4c3b-8131-7afc3f1cc303")
	)
	(text "Sound: I2S (64 BCK a frame, 48,828 Hz) into a PCM5102A; SCK tied low:\nthe DAC's PLL makes its clock from BCK. FMT low = I2S. XSMT high = unmuted.\nLine out through a 470R / 2.2nF filter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110 100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3ab2f79f-a7ff-45a5-a21e-56ead66fe910")
	)
	(text "PS/2 mouse (the keyboard uses the board's own PS/2 port, M15/M16).\nOpen drain both ways: the FPGA drives low or lets go. BSS138 level\nshifters (gate at 3.3 V); 10k pull-ups on both sides. Not 5 V tolerant!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245 92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4a085c16-f9aa-4ae4-b899-044d18ae00ac")
	)
	(text "fpga_cpu: Spartan-3 Starter Board expansion (rough). Serial and the keyboard\nare on the board itself (DB9: RXD T13, TXD R13; PS/2: M15/M16)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5dcd70f5-8ff0-41fa-863c-6b6a95908c01")
	)
	(text "NOR flash ROM, executed in place (a resident toolbox: no RAM spent on it).\nThe part: SST39VF1601C-70 (1M x 16, 3.3 V, TSOP-48), DQ0-DQ7 used: 512 KB.\nIts A0-A18 as shown, A19 to GND, DQ8-DQ15 open (pulled up in the FPGA's\nsimulation only), WP#/RST# to 3.3 V. (The symbol is a stand-in: KiCad has\nnone for it; the connections are the same by name.) CE# pulled up:\noff while the FPGA configures. Writes (programming) use the JEDEC command\nsequences through the same bus, with a long WE# pulse."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110 225 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "762f9d54-2157-49d4-8c6d-bb1aa1f46049")
	)
	(text "WiFi: ESP32-WROOM-32E (e.g. ESP-AT firmware) on its own pins, not the SD bus:\nshared, the ESP's MISO would be GPIO12, a strap the SD pull-up would hold high\n(1.8 V flash: no boot). VSPI slave: SCK IO18, MOSI IO23, MISO IO19, CS IO5;\nIO4 = handshake/interrupt to the FPGA; EN (reset) and IO0 (download mode)\ndriven by the FPGA (open drain; pull-ups, EN RC). UART1 (IO16 in, IO17 out)\nto the FPGA too; UART0 on J8 for flashing. Own AMS1117 from +5V: the module\ndraws ~500 mA when transmitting. One SPI engine in the FPGA serves SD and WiFi."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 318 100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "95d55897-c3e8-4a32-aef0-c4671216fa12")
	)
	(text "microSD in SPI mode: DAT3 = CS, CMD = MOSI, DAT0 = MISO; DAT1/DAT2 pulled\nup (unused); card detect to the FPGA. 47k pull-ups, 33R on the clock."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110 185 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b2425a49-3c93-4829-b526-e138fa040c0c")
	)
	(text "Sega Genesis / Mega Drive pads (3- and 6-button) on DE9 plugs, at 5 V\n(each through a 500 mA polyfuse). One select (TH) for both pads, driven\nat 5 V by U7; 100R to each port. The 12 inputs come back through two\n74LVC245A at 3.3 V (5 V-tolerant inputs): the Spartan-3's pins are not.\nTH high: UP DOWN LEFT RIGHT B C; TH low: UP DOWN 0 0 A Start. A 6-button\npad answers its 3rd low with UP..RIGHT all 0, and its 4th high with\nZ Y X Mode; it resets 1.5 ms after the last pulse. Software reads both pads.\nWith TH low, LEFT and RIGHT at 1 (the pull-ups): no pad."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430 255 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "beea09cc-143c-4272-b09e-64a38f351210")
	)
	(text "J3 needs a mini-DIN-6 footprint (e.g. CUI MD-60S): none in KiCad's library."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.426 233.934 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cdd59db5-b201-4153-b440-4bdf7e513da6")
	)
	(text "A2 expansion connector (UG130 table 13-3)\n4 E6 I2S_BCK   5 D5 I2S_LRCK   6 C5 I2S_DATA\n7 D6 MS_CLK    8 C6 MS_DATA\n9 E7 SD_CS    10 C7 SD_SCK   11 D7 SD_MOSI\n12 C8 SD_MISO 13 D8 SD_CD\n14 C9 PAD_SEL (out)  15 D10 PAD1_UP 16 A3 PAD1_DOWN 17 B4 PAD1_LEFT\n27 B10 PAD1_RIGHT 28 A10 PAD1_TL 29 B11 PAD1_TR 30 B12 PAD2_UP\n31 A12 PAD2_DOWN 32 B13 PAD2_LEFT 33 A13 PAD2_RIGHT 34 B14 PAD2_TL\n35 D9 PAD2_TR (the oscillator socket's pin: leave the socket empty)\n18 A4 WIFI_CS 19 B5 WIFI_SCK 20 A5 WIFI_MOSI 21 B6 WIFI_MISO\n22 B7 WIFI_HS 23 A7 WIFI_EN 24 B8 WIFI_BOOT 25 A8 WIFI_TXD 26 A9 WIFI_RXD\n36-40 configuration: leave open\n2 +5V (VU), 3 +3.3V (VCCO), 1 GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 115 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f5998824-b6bc-473f-932b-6c77b2ea15cc")
	)
